WEBVTT

00:00:00.757 --> 00:00:03.066
A country… inside another country?

00:00:03.891 --> 00:00:07.609
Hidden completely inside South
Africa is the kingdom of Lesotho.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.868
And unlike most countries,

00:00:10.207 --> 00:00:14.402
Lesotho has no coastline — and
no border with any other country.

00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:17.542
It's also one of the
highest countries on Earth.

00:00:18.614 --> 00:00:19.923
So how did this happen?

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.825
Lesotho survived as the Basotho
kingdom — under British protection —

00:00:26.277 --> 00:00:29.564
while European colonial powers
divided much of southern Africa.

00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:33.058
When South Africa's borders
eventually formed around it,

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.422
Lesotho remained a separate country.

00:00:36.301 --> 00:00:39.679
Today, more than two million people
live in this mountain kingdom.

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:44.401
It's one of only three countries in the
world completely surrounded by another

00:00:44.401 --> 00:00:45.401
country.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.597
Geography is wild.
